<section class="panel" aria-label="Independently authored subtraction representation tasks"><h2>Subtraction Algorithms (Part 1) — Grade 3 Unit 3 Lesson 8</h2><p>Connect drawings of base-ten units with a written subtraction algorithm. Use base-ten blocks or a number line. A teacher reviews strategies, original graphics and discussion.</p><h3>Warm-up: Number Talk: Subtraction Strategies (10 minutes)</h3><p>Source-context mathematical checks (write your reasoning separately):</p><ol><li>100 - 98</li><li>101 - 99</li><li>200 - 98</li><li>204 - 98</li></ol><p>Discuss patterns or make a mental number talk before checking.</p><h3>Activity 1: From Drawings to an Algorithm (15 minutes)</h3><p>Source-context mathematical checks (write your reasoning separately):</p><ol><li>391-215</li></ol><p>Use a strategy or algorithm that fits, then justify steps.</p><h3>Activity 2: Card Sort: Diagrams and Algorithms (20 minutes)</h3><p>Source-context mathematical checks (write your reasoning separately):</p><ol></ol><p>Compare source drawings or written records with a partner; the teacher checks the match.</p><h3>Visuals and explanation — teacher review</h3><ul><li>Explain how Kiran decomposes a ten and changes the written ones position before subtracting 391−215.</li><li>Match source diagram cards with subtraction algorithm cards; actual publisher cards or approved alternatives are required.</li><li>Discuss why the drawings and written representations describe the same trade of one ten for ten ones.</li></ul><h3>Method and access</h3><p>The warm-up considers 100−98=2,101−99=2,200−98=102 and204−98=106. Relate 391−215=176 to the base-ten drawing: the 1 one is insufficient to remove 5 ones, so a ten is exchanged for ten ones (391 becomes 3 hundreds,8 tens,11 ones). The first steps in Kiran's written subtraction should show the corresponding regrouping. An original deck of base-ten diagrams must be matched with written subtraction algorithms; these are teacher-evaluated matching and explanation tasks, not scalar checks. The original deck and image bytes were not accessed and are not drawn as if identical.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-3/lesson-8/lesson.html">2021 official public teacher lesson</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-3/lesson-8/preparation.html">Official preparation and Student Task Statements link</a>. Source PDF/illustration parity is unverified. Original gated Cool-down is NOT reproduced.</p></section>
